WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.904
The colour is not in the tube.

2
00:00:02.064 --> 00:00:06.290
Look at a brick, a leaf or a pebble and you will not find that colour in any tube.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.936
Real colours are mixed.

4
00:00:08.096 --> 00:00:12.229
Matching means mixing, holding it up, and changing it until it looks right.

5
00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:14.740
White, black and the opposite.

6
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.315
Three changes do three different jobs.

7
00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:19.658
White lightens a colour into a tint.

8
00:00:19.818 --> 00:00:21.815
Black darkens it into a shade.

9
00:00:21.975 --> 00:00:26.851
A little of the opposite colour on the wheel makes it duller without making it lighter or darker.

10
00:00:27.551 --> 00:00:28.805
A tone ladder.

11
00:00:28.965 --> 00:00:32.541
Mix a colour, then mix it again with a little more white each time.

12
00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:35.394
Line the steps up and you have a ladder of tones.

13
00:00:35.554 --> 00:00:38.712
Now you can find the exact tone you need instead of guessing.

14
00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:40.945
Paint behaves differently.

15
00:00:41.105 --> 00:00:43.566
Watercolour is see-through, so it washes.

16
00:00:43.726 --> 00:00:45.212
Poster paint covers.

17
00:00:45.372 --> 00:00:50.016
Oil pastel is waxy, so paint slides off it and the mark stays white.

18
00:00:50.176 --> 00:00:53.334
Ink makes a fine, strong line on top of dry paint.
